sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor E as Employee
    participant K as Kiosk or ESS
    participant V as Aadhaar token store
    actor C as Compliance checker
    participant P as ESIC portal
    participant A as Audit log

    E->>K: Chooses to let the employer seed Aadhaar at IP registration
    K->>E: Regulation 5 notice with purpose, voluntary status and the alternative
    E->>K: Grants in writing for AADHAAR_ESIC_IP_SEEDING
    E->>K: Types the number in a private session
    K->>V: PUT over an encrypted channel with the grant id
    V->>A: PUT recorded with token and purpose, never the number
    V-->>K: Opaque token and last four digits
    C->>V: REVEAL_FOR_PURPOSE naming the open IP registration task
    V->>A: Reveal recorded with actor, role, task, grant and NTP time
    V-->>C: Number shown in the task view for the reveal window only
    C->>P: Keys the number during IP registration, an employer act
    P-->>C: IP number allotted after the portal authenticates
    C->>V: IP number recorded and approved, purpose spent
    V->>V: PURGE within the purge lag, entry key destroyed
    V->>A: Purge recorded with its basis, reg 6 sub-regulation 5
    V-->>K: Token now resolves to a tombstone

    Note over C,P: Our operator never reveals or keys a number
